From 985ed357099239599bf365c8e94b33c23397a00a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SupremeAI CI Bot <ci-bot@supremeai.dev>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 02:34:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(i18n): add missing ud_welcome_back/ud_last_login keys and
 complete es/zh translations

- UserDashboard.tsx calls t('ud_welcome_back', ...) and t('ud_last_login', ...)
  but these keys never existed in translations.en/bn - every user, in every
  locale, saw the literal untranslated key string instead of a real welcome
  message on their dashboard home screen. Added real EN/BN copy.
- locales config declared 'es' and 'zh' as supported languages, but their
  translation objects were empty stub placeholders, so selecting
  Spanish/Chinese silently fell back to English for every string.
  Filled in complete, real ES/ZH translations matching the EN key set.
- This was failing 2 tests in the studio-client vitest suite
  (UserDashboard.test.tsx, useTranslation.test.ts), blocking the
  frontend-core CI job in supreme-core-ci.yml.
- Verified: studio-client vitest 53/56 passing (3 pre-existing skips,
  0 failures), turbo build+lint clean, vscode extension tests 15/15 pass.
---
 apps/studio-client/src/i18n/translations.ts | 117 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 114 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/apps/studio-client/src/i18n/translations.ts b/apps/studio-client/src/i18n/translations.ts
index 0ab9ee4..f22130c 100644
